    "description": {
     "value": "<p>A two-handed blade as tall as its wielder, hammered from a pre-Fall highway sign-post or a faction forge's best sheet. Slow to bring around, impossible to ignore. Favoured by gate-wardens and anyone whose job is to make the first person through a door regret it.</p><p>Heavy two-handed kinetic. No signature — the weight is the statement.</p>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p>\n<p>Two-handed, heavy. Pairs well with a Bulwark's Surge. No signature ability.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d12 + 1 Kinetic damage to <em>Integrity</em> <span style=\"opacity:.75\">(blade)</span></li>\n  <li><strong>Faculty:</strong> Violence</li>\n  <li><strong>Attack:</strong> Melee (Violence)</li>\n  <li><strong>Reach:</strong> Melee</li>\n  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier:</strong> T2</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:END -->\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⟡ Inlaid (+1). Hex-inlay along the working edge.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>+1 to hit and +1 damage</strong> with this weapon (the hit bonus is read from the weapon you swing).</li>\n  <li>Grade raises it to <strong>Tier II</strong> · free to wield.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:END -->"
    }
