    "description": {
     "value": "<p>A straight double-edged blade with a plain cross-guard and a grip long enough for a second hand. Ground from pre-Fall leaf-spring or Domain tab-steel, depending on who made it and what they had. The weapon most hex militias train on first, because it forgives bad footwork and rewards good.</p><p>No signature, no hum, no history worth mentioning. It cuts.</p>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⚙️ Mechanical Effects</strong></p>\n<p>Versatile: one hand beside a shield, two hands when you mean it. No signature ability.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Damage:</strong> 1d8 + 1 Kinetic damage to <em>Integrity</em> <span style=\"opacity:.75\">(blade)</span></li>\n  <li><strong>Faculty:</strong> Violence</li>\n  <li><strong>Attack:</strong> Melee (Violence)</li>\n  <li><strong>Reach:</strong> Melee</li>\n  <li><strong>Duration:</strong> Scene</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier:</strong> T2</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:MECHANICS:END -->\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:START -->\n<hr/>\n<p><strong>⟡ Inlaid (+1). Hex-inlay along the working edge.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>+1 to hit and +1 damage</strong> with this weapon (the hit bonus is read from the weapon you swing).</li>\n  <li>Grade raises it to <strong>Tier II</strong> · free to wield.</li>\n</ul>\n<!-- BBTTCC:LADDER:END -->"
    }
